# Tracer: the double-underscore prefix is reserved for generated output.
#
# Before (worked as user syntax):
# have __x R = 1
# __x = 1
# Former behavior: double-underscore names occupied the same namespace as generated output.
#
# Now (verified):
have _x R = 1
_x = 1
# Current behavior: one leading underscore remains valid user syntax.
#
# Boundary: `have __x R = 1` and every longer underscore prefix are rejected.
# The tokenizer regression test covers this reserved-prefix boundary.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -isolated -f examples/03_language_features/reserved_internal_symbol_prefix.lit
# Negative CLI: target/release/litex -e 'have __x R = 1' (expected parse error)
# Negative regression: tests/unit/parsing/tokenizer/tests.rs
